#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/magnify-a-screen-area.md:0
msgid ""
"Turn on the zoom feature to magnify part of the screen in Ubuntu Desktop, "
"and adjust magnification, mouse tracking, crosshairs and colors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/magnify-a-screen-area.md:7
msgid "Topics: Accessibility"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/magnify-a-screen-area.md:11
msgid "Magnify a screen area"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/magnify-a-screen-area.md:13
msgid ""
"Magnifying the screen is different than just enlarging the {ref}`text size "
"<change-text-size-on-the-screen>`. This feature is like having a magnifying "
"glass, allowing you to move around by zooming in on parts of the screen."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/magnify-a-screen-area.md:15
msgid "Open the Activities overview and start typing **accessibility**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/magnify-a-screen-area.md:16
msgid "Click {guilabel}`Accessibility` to open the panel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/magnify-a-screen-area.md:17
msgid "Open the {guilabel}`Zoom` section."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/magnify-a-screen-area.md:18
msgid "Enable the {guilabel}`Desktop Zoom` option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/magnify-a-screen-area.md:20
msgid ""
"You can now move around the screen area. By moving your mouse to the edges "
"of the screen, you will move the magnified area in different directions, "
"allowing you to view your area of choice."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/magnify-a-screen-area.md:23
msgid ""
"You can quickly turn zoom on and off by clicking the {ref}`accessibility "
"icon <find-the-accessibility-menu>` on the top bar and selecting {guilabel}"
"`Zoom`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/magnify-a-screen-area.md:26
msgid ""
"You can change the magnification factor, the mouse tracking, and the "
"position of the magnified view on the screen. Adjust these in the {guilabel}"
"`Magnifier` section."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/magnify-a-screen-area.md:28
msgid ""
"You can activate crosshairs to help you find the mouse or touchpad pointer. "
"Switch them on and adjust their length, color, and thickness in the "
"{guilabel}`Crosshairs` section."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/magnify-a-screen-area.md:30
msgid ""
"You can switch to inverted colors video, and adjust brightness, contrast and "
"color options for the magnifier in the {guilabel}`Color Filters` section. "
"The combination of these options is useful for people with low-vision, any "
"degree of photophobia, or just for using the computer under adverse lighting "
"conditions."
msgstr ""
